is.edu\nStay Connected\nAlumni\nAlumni Awards\nDistinguished Alumni Awards\nMarcia Peterman ECE Award\nYoung Alumni Achievement Award\nAlumni Board\nPast Board Members\nPast Graduate Student Representatives\nAlumni Events\nAlumni News\nVirtual Yearbook\nGive Back\nClass of 2026\nPlan Your Visit\nStay Connected\nGiving\nContact Us\nHeather Vazquez\nSenior Director of Advancement\n1060 ECE Building\n(217) 333-2517\nhfv@illinois.edu\nGiving\nECE Visionary Scholarship Donors\nWays to Give\nGiving Stories\nEndowments\nInclusion\nInclusion\nBroadening Participation in ECE\nStudent Wellness Resources\nHome\nAdmissions\nGraduate Admissions\nPh.D. Admissions\nPh.D. Admissions\nElectrical and Computer Engineering Ph.D. Program Information\nBecome an expert and continue breaking boundaries.\nAt the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at the University of Illinois, we empower our students to break boundaries in knowledge, research and innovation. Admission to our Ph.D. program will place you among mentors and peers who are continuously setting new records in academic and research excellence. Discover how you can join our collaborative and interdisciplinary community.\nOn this page\nHow to Apply\nImportant Dates\nFields of Specialization\nHow to Apply\nReview minimum admission requirements, listed by country.\nComplete the online application through The Graduate College. Select \"Electrical and Computer Engineering\u2014PHD.\" Students who are unable to apply online must contact graduate admissions.\nSubmit an ECE Graduate Applicant Preferences Form to indicate your areas of research interest. Forms are available two days after submitting applications.\nView all admissions requirements and processes\nImportant Admissions Dates\nApplications are submitted through the Graduate Application Portal. Please select \"Electrical and Computer Engineering\u2014PHD.\" All materials, credentials, and test scores must be received by midnight Eastern Standard Time (EST).\nApplications are due:\nJanuary 15 for the fall semester (Apply by December 15 for complete consideration for fellowships and awards)\nSeptember 1 for the spring semester.\nAdmission decisions for ECE Ph.D. programs are typically announced by April 2 for summer/fall admissions. In some cases, however, decisions may be reached much earlier.\nApply Now\nFields of Specialization\nMachine Learning, AI and Data Science\nNetworking, Mobile and Distributed Computing\nRobotics, Autonomy, Control and Cyber-Physical Systems\nComputer Architecture, Circuits and Systems\nSignal Processing, Biomedical Imaging and Acoustics\nMicroelectronics, Photonics and Nanotechnology\nPower and Energy Systems\nFind detailed information on ECE research areas and cross-cutting themes.\nReady to Apply?\nBegin Graduate Application\nElectrical & Computer Engineering\nTwitter\nInstagram\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\nYouTube\n306 N. Wright St. MC 702\nUrbana, IL 61801\nPhone: 217-333-2300\nFax:\nEmail:\nThe Grainger College of Engineering\nGet In Touch\nMake a Gift\nExplore\nAlums: Connect with us\nBuildings and facilities\nRoom reservations\nHistory\nJobs\nDaily Byte Cafe\nECE Supply Center\nElectronics Services Shop\nContact Us\nE-mail ECE ILLINOIS\nVisit Campus\nAbout Cookies\nPrivacy Policy\nCopyright \u00a9 2026\nAccessibility\nWebmaster\nLogin", "links": [["Block I logo University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign", "https://illinois.edu/?utm_source=electricalcomputerengineering&utm_medium=web&utm_campaign=header"], ["Apply", "https://admissions.illinois.edu/Home/myillini-apply"], ["Give", "https://www.givecampus.com/campaigns/49289/donations/new"], ["My.ECE", "https://my.ece.illinois.edu"], ["The Grainger College of Engineering", "https://grainger.illinois.edu"], ["Electrical & Computer Engineering", "https://ece.illinois.edu/"], ["Search", "https://ece.illinois.edu/search"], ["About", "https://ece.illinois.edu/about"], ["Where is it?", "https://www.google.com/maps/dir/40.1006592,-88.236032/306+N.+Wright+St.+MC+7